2) Relevantna literatura
	A. Obavezno pročitati (jezgro rada)
		1. Jimenez et al. (2024) — SWE-bench: Can Language Models Resolve Real-World GitHub Issues? — ICLR 2024
			https://arxiv.org/abs/2310.06770
			Dataset i evaluaciona procedura rada.
		2. Yang et al. (2024) — SWE-agent: Agent-Computer Interfaces Enable Automated Software Engineering — NeurIPS 2024
			https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.15793
			Najvažniji prior work. Uvodi ACI koncept, radi ablaciju interfejsa na SWE-bench Lite — direktan prior work za H2.
		3. Xia et al. (2024) — Agentless: Demystifying LLM-based Software Engineering Agents — FSE 2025
			https://arxiv.org/abs/2407.01489
			Kritično za H1. Tvrde da složeni agenti nisu potrebni — trofazni pipeline postiže 32.00% (96 tačnih fixeva) uz nisku cenu ($0.70) na SWE-bench Lite, nadmašujući postojeće open-source agente. Praktično ista teza ("minimalan set je dovoljan") dokazana iz drugog ugla — obavezno pozicionirati se prema njoj. Takođe prave SWE-bench Lite-S izbacivanjem problematičnih instanci — relevantno za brigu oko kvaliteta podataka.
		4. Aleithan et al. (2024) — SWE-Bench+: Enhanced Coding Benchmark for LLMs
			https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.06992
			Dokumentuje solution leakage (32.67%) i slabe testove u SWE-bench. Za poglavlje o ograničenjima.
		5. Phan et al. (2024) — HyperAgent: Generalist Software Engineering Agents to Solve Coding Tasks at Scale
			https://arxiv.org/abs/2409.16299
			Ablacija po alatima i po ulogama agenta, meri i cost i resolve rate — najbliži primer metodologije ovog rada.
		6. Wang et al. (2024) — OpenHands: An Open Platform for AI Software Developers as Generalist Agents — ICLR 2025
			https://arxiv.org/abs/2407.16741
			Referentni open-source harness — objašnjava zašto je pravljen sopstveni (potreba za kontrolom nad tool setom).
		7. Yao et al. (2023) — ReAct: Synergizing Reasoning and Acting in Language Models — ICLR 2023
			https://arxiv.org/abs/2210.03629
			Temeljna paradigma tool-using agenata. Poglavlje 3.2.
		8. Schick et al. (2023) — Toolformer: Language Models Can Teach Themselves to Use Tools — NeurIPS 2023
			https://arxiv.org/abs/2302.04761
			Temeljni rad o tool learning-u. Poglavlje 3.2.

